From 5c7162a73f1e7301ff3a7ca9b9c16073c7eeeee5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:04:55 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] batched GPU painting of widgets behind
 QT_WIDGETS_GPU_PAINT=batch: a recording paint engine in Qt Gui

The engine records rectangles, glyphs and pictures as instances of one quad, cut to the
clip on the CPU and kept in paint order; the window's RHI compositor frame draws them in
one call per blend mode into a texture that keeps the window's contents. Anything else is
drawn by the raster engine into a scratch image and laid over in order, counted by kind.
QT_WIDGETS_GPU_PAINT=1 (or opengl) stays the first path, for comparing.

