+// Copyright (C) 2026 Daniel Campos Ramos
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-Qt-Commercial OR LGPL-3.0-only OR GPL-2.0-only OR GPL-3.0-only
+
+/*
+    A backing store whose widgets are painted on the GPU in batches (behind
+    QT_WIDGETS_GPU_PAINT=batch).
+
+    The paint engine draws nothing while the widgets paint: it records. Every fill of a
+    rectangle, every glyph and every picture becomes one small record (a rectangle on the
+    target, a rectangle in a texture, a colour), cut to the clip on the CPU and kept in paint
+    order. When the window is flushed, the records are uploaded as one buffer and drawn as
+    instances of one quad by one shader, into a texture that keeps the window's contents, inside
+    the frame the window's RHI compositor has open. So a paint pass costs a few draw calls,
+    however many things it painted.
+
+    Text comes from one texture of glyph masks, the masks the raster engine itself blends (the
+    font engine's, at the same parts of a pixel), placed on whole pixels and taken unfiltered,
+    so text is what CPU painting gives at every scale. Pictures come from one texture of small
+    pictures; large ones are copied for the frame.
+
+    What is not a rectangle, a glyph or a picture (paths, lines, gradients, rotated things) is
+    drawn by the raster engine, the same call with the same state, into a transparent part of a
+    scratch image, which is uploaded with the frame and laid over the target in order. The engine
+    counts these by kind, so what is not covered is known (QT_WIDGETS_PAINT_STATS=1 prints the
+    counts; the logging category qt.gui.batchpaint names each kind once).
+*/
+
